#: includes/views/help-tab.php:29
msgid "Everything you can do with QuickShipD"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:31
msgid "QuickShipD works out when an order will arrive and shows it to the customer before they buy. Nothing here needs installing, it is all live already."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:34
msgid "Help sections"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:52
msgid "Set your delivery window"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:53
msgid "On the Delivery tab, enter the minimum and maximum days a parcel takes to arrive after you hand it to the carrier. Set both to the same number for a single date instead of a range. Use 0 for same-day delivery."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:56
msgid "Set your order cutoff"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:57
msgid "Orders placed before this time go out the same day. Anything after it moves to the next dispatch day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:60
msgid "Tick your non-dispatch days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:61
msgid "The weekdays you do not send orders out, usually Saturday and Sunday. They are never counted toward the estimate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:64
msgid "Add your holidays"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:65
msgid "Single dates or date ranges you are closed. Tick \"Repeats every year\" for fixed holidays such as Christmas."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:68
msgid "Choose where it appears"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:69
msgid "The Display tab controls product pages, shop archives, cart, and checkout. The Style tab controls wording and colours. The live preview updates as you type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:80
msgid "How the date is worked out"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:83
msgid "QuickShipD keeps the day you dispatch separate from the days a parcel spends in transit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:88
msgid "Start from today"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:89
msgid "If the cutoff time has already passed, move to tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:93
msgid "Find the dispatch day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:94
msgid "If that day is a non-dispatch day or a holiday, roll forward until it is not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:98
msgid "Count the transit days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:99
msgid "Count forward from the dispatch day, skipping non-dispatch days and holidays."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:104
msgid "Worked example"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:105
msgid "Weekends off, delivery 1 to 2 days, a customer orders on Saturday. Nothing ships at the weekend, so the dispatch day rolls to Monday. One to two days after Monday gives Tuesday to Wednesday. Monday is never shown as the arrival date, because that is the day the parcel leaves you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:108
msgid "The countdown is hidden on days you do not dispatch, because beating the cutoff on those days cannot change the date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:117
msgid "Where the estimate shows"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:122
msgid "Product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:123
msgid "Full estimate with icon and the cutoff countdown. Variable products update as the shopper picks a variation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:126
msgid "Shop and archives"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:126
msgid "off by default"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:127
msgid "Compact estimate, no countdown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:130
msgid "Cart"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:131
msgid "An \"Est. Delivery\" line under each item. Works on the classic and the block cart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:134
msgid "Checkout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:135
msgid "A summary row above shipping on the classic checkout. On the block checkout the per-item line shows instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:138
msgid "Emails and orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:139
msgid "Saved onto the order line at checkout, so it stays fixed on the order record in emails, admin orders, and My Account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:154
msgid "Place the estimate yourself anywhere on the site. This is the answer whenever a page builder such as Elementor or Divi builds its own product layout, never fires the standard WooCommerce hooks, and the estimate does not appear on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:159
#: includes/views/help-tab.php:192
#: includes/views/help-tab.php:199
#: includes/views/help-tab.php:206
msgid "Copy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:162
msgid "Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:167
msgid "Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:168
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:169
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:175
msgid "current product"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:176
msgid "Which product to estimate for. Leave it out on a product page or inside a product loop and the current product is used. Required anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:181
msgid "Which style to use. \"product\" gives the full estimate with countdown, \"shop\" gives the compact one without."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:186
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:194
msgid "On a product page or in an Elementor product template. Picks up the product on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:201
msgid "On a landing page, a widget, or any page that is not a product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:208
msgid "Compact style with no countdown, for tight layouts and product grids."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:212
msgid "The shortcode respects every setting on the other tabs, including per-product overrides. It outputs nothing for a product that is out of stock or has QuickShipD switched off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:221
msgid "Text placeholders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:224
msgid "Drop these into the message templates on the Style tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:229
msgid "The single or latest delivery date"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:233
msgid "The earliest date in a range"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:237
msgid "The latest date in a range"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:241
msgid "Time left before the order cutoff"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:255
msgid "The Delivery tab sets the store default. Two things can override it, in this order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:259
msgid "1. Per product"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:260
msgid "Edit a product, open the Shipping tab in Product data, and set its own minimum and maximum days. You can also switch QuickShipD off for that product entirely."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:263
msgid "2. Per shipping method"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:264
msgid "In WooCommerce, Settings, Shipping, open a zone and edit a method. Each method has its own minimum and maximum, so express can quote a faster date than standard. Leave blank to use the store default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:279
msgid "It does not show on my product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:280
msgid "Check the product is in stock and that QuickShipD is not switched off on it. If the page is built with Elementor, Divi, or another builder, the theme never fires the WooCommerce hook, so drop the [quickshipd] shortcode into the layout where you want it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:284
msgid "The dates on my site do not match the preview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:285
msgid "Both use your WordPress timezone from Settings, General. If they still differ, a page cache is most likely serving an older copy of the page. Clear it and check again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:289
msgid "The countdown is missing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:290
msgid "The countdown only appears on product pages, only when it is switched on, and only before the cutoff on a day you actually dispatch. After the cutoff there is nothing left to count down to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:294
msgid "Changing shipping method did not change the date"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:295
msgid "Method overrides only apply at cart and checkout, where a method has actually been chosen. Product pages always use the store default, since no method is selected yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:305
msgid "Good to know"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:309
msgid "Dates are worked out in PHP on page load. No external services are contacted and no customer data leaves your site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:310
msgid "Frontend CSS and JavaScript load only on pages that actually show an estimate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:311
msgid "Compatible with HPOS and the block cart and checkout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:312
msgid "Restore Defaults at the bottom of this page resets every setting, including holidays and non-dispatch days."
msgstr ""

